    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0840" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.00/10–947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-09">October 9,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>416. Cite Zpol 1239. Adopted four resolutions
                    which were released to press by Rhee on October 7th.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d633-f1"/> Text follows in Seoul PolAd No. 417, October 9th.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d633-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Department will note threats contained in these resolutions which may mean that
                    Rhee is determined to force US to hold an election before decision is reached at
                    UN or to compel US to take action against him so that he can appear in the light
                    of a martyr. He and his group are alone in agitating for a South Korean election
                    before Korea question is considered by UN. Even Kim Koo and his group are not
                    supporting Rhee in this.</p>
                <pb facs="0841" n="827" xml:id="pg827"/>
                <p>It may also be observed that since subsidence of leftist activities about middle
                    of August, the chief cause of disorder in South Korea has been the strong armed
                    methods of Rhee’s rightist groups especially by his youth corps.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacobs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d633-f1" n="35" xml:id="d633-f1-content">
                <p>Adopted by Rhee’s “Korean National Association” on October 6.</p>
            </note>
